<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Emir Abdelkader</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1808">1808</a>–<a href="/years/1883">1883</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Abd al-Qadir al-Jazairi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emir">Emir</a> Abdelkader was an Algerian religious and military leader who led resistance to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-conquest-of-algeria">French conquest of Algeria</a> from 1832 to 1847. Chosen as emir by the tribes of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algeria">Algeria</a>, he built a state with its own administration, taxes and army, and was recognised by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> in the treaties of Desmichels and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tafna">Tafna</a>. He surrendered in 1847, was held in France, and in exile in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/damascus">Damascus</a> protected thousands of Christians during the massacre of 1860.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/emir-abdelkader.jpg" alt="Emir Abdelkader" width="320" height="503" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ange Tissier · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%A3%D9%85%D9%8A%D8%B1_%D8%B9%D8%A8%D8%AF_%D8%A7%D9%84%D9%82%D8%A7%D8%AF%D8%B1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>…the east Ahmed Bey of Constantine, whose city fell in 1837 after a failed first assault in 1836, and in the west the Emirate of <b>Abdelkader</b>, which France recognised in the Treaty of Desmichels in 1834 and the Treaty of Tafna in 1837 before war resumed in 1839.</blockquote><a href="/empire/french-algeria">French Algeria · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>After France conquered Algiers and the Beylik of the West collapsed, the tribes of western Algeria chose the young Sufi scholar <b>Abdelkader</b> as their emir near Mascara in 1832.</blockquote><a href="/state/emirate-of-abdelkader">Emirate of Abdelkader</a></li></ul></section>
